The property is on the secondary market, and the given history identifies one transaction preceding the current purchase, so the listed annual tariff is 0.20 per 100 rubles, or 0.20%. The prior transaction was more than three years ago, giving the listed 1.2 coefficient. The missing required dispensary certificates give the 0.8 coefficient for absence of a necessary document. No listed facts trigger the first corrective-factor row, whose coefficient is not supplied in the provided table. Applying the specified tariff and coefficients, the annual premium is 14,500,000\times0.002\times1.2\times0.8=27,840 rubles.
FINAL_ANSWER: \boxed{27,840\text{ rubles per year, on an insured amount of }14,500,000\text{ rubles}}

Let the square have side s and place A at a corner with its sides along the coordinate axes. Since the circle is tangent to AB and AD, its center is distance r from each, and tangency points on those sides are r from A. The given 8 cm segments from B and D therefore give s−r=8, or s=r+8.
On the opposite sides, the perpendicular distance from the center to either side is also s−r=8. A circle centered symmetrically with respect to the two sides cuts equal lengths from the corresponding vertices on those opposite sides: each such length is r−√(r²−64) (when intersections exist). The problem assigns these cutoffs as 4 cm and 2 cm, which are unequal. This contradicts the symmetry, so no circle satisfies all the stated conditions.
FINAL_ANSWER: \boxed{\text{no such circle exists}}

