The sums c+d and c+e must be among the listed values. They sum to (7+d)+(7+e)=36, and the only pair of listed values summing to 36 is 16 and 20. Hence d=9 and e=13. But then the two pair sums a+d and b+d add to a+b+2d=-1+18=17. No two members of the supplied list sum to 17. This contradiction shows that the supplied set cannot be the pair sums of five integers, so the requested product does not exist.
