With eight nonattacking rooks on an 8 by 8 board, there must be exactly one rook in each row and each column. A square is white precisely when its row and column have the same parity (with aligned indexing of rows and columns). Thus the four even rows must be matched bijectively to the four even columns, and the four odd rows to the four odd columns. Each matching has 4! choices, independently.

Therefore the count is (4!)²=576.
FINAL_ANSWER: \boxed{576}

Since CD is an altitude to AB and D lies on AB, triangle BDC is right-angled at D. Its hypotenuse BC is 12 and angle CBD equals angle ABC, or 30 degrees. Therefore BD=12 cos 30°=6√3.
DE is the altitude from the right angle of triangle BDC to its hypotenuse BC. By the right-triangle projection theorem, BD²=BE·BC. Thus BE=(6√3)²/12=108/12=9.
