Label the vertices 0,...,15 cyclically. Chord direction is determined by i+j modulo 16. For each odd residue k, the condition i+j≡k gives 8 disjoint chords, hence C(8,2)=28 pairs of parallel sides. For each even k it gives 7 chords (the two fixed vertices of i↦k-i yield no chord), hence 21 pairs. Across 8 residues of each parity this counts 8·28+8·21=392 trapezoids, counting by a chosen pair of parallel opposite sides.
The only quadrilaterals counted twice have both opposite side pairs parallel, so are rectangles. Each inscribed rectangle is determined by choosing two of the 8 diameters, giving C(8,2)=28. Subtracting these duplicates gives 364, allowing rectangles as trapezoids.
FINAL_ANSWER: \boxed{364}

Use coordinates A=(0,0), B=(0,b), C=(c,0), so the right angle is at A; write M=(m,0). Since D is the midpoint of BC, D=(c/2,b/2). The angle AMB has tangent b/m, while angle CMD has tangent (b/2)/(c/2−m)=b/(c−2m). The given equality of angles therefore yields m=c−2m, so m=c/3.
Then BM²=b²+(c/3)², whereas MD²=(b/2)²+(c/6)²=BM²/4. Consequently BM/MD=2.
