Momentum conservation gives m u+M v=−m u/2+M V. Substituting V yields (3/2)m u=(3/2)M(u−v), hence v/u=1−m/M. Since the problem specifies m much smaller than M, this ratio is approximately 1: the requested initial velocities are approximately equal. An exact numerical ratio is not determined without the mass ratio.
